---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../data/site';

const effective = 'October 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Terms for using ${SITE_NAME}, its articles, directory and OrbitFleet simulators, and for donations.`}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-display font-bold mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 mb-10">Effective {effective}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-a:text-mars-red hover:prose-a:text-mars-rust">
      <p>
        These terms apply to populationmars.com, orbitfleet.populationmars.com and related pages (the
        "sites") run by {SITE_NAME} ("we", "us"). By using the sites you agree to them. If you do not
        agree, please do not use the sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Educational and research content</h2>
      <p>
        Articles, the Mars atlas, the space economy directory and the OrbitFleet simulators are provided
        for education and research. Simulations use public, proposed, configured or synthetic data and
        approximate physics, and each view labels which. Nothing on the sites is an operational
        collision warning, navigation product, mission telemetry, engineering certification, or
        investment, legal or financial advice. Do not rely on it for safety-critical or financial
        decisions.
      </p>

      <h2>Directory listings</h2>
      <p>
        The space economy directory is an independent editorial selection. Inclusion is not an
        endorsement, and company descriptions and funding figures come from public sources that may
        change. Some links may be partner or affiliate links; when they are, we say so near the link.
        Listing requests are reviewed editorially and may be declined or edited. To request a correction,
        email <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Donations</h2>
      <p>
        Donations are voluntary gifts that support our research and publishing. They are processed by
        Stripe and do not buy goods, services, equity or any other interest in {SITE_NAME}.
        {SITE_NAME} is not currently a registered charity, so donations are generally not tax-deductible;
        please consult your tax adviser. Monthly gifts can be cancelled at any time from your Stripe
        receipt or by emailing us. Because donations fund work already in progress, they are generally
        non-refundable, but if you made a mistake, contact us within 14 days and we will try to help.
      </p>

      <h2>Investment inquiries</h2>
      <p>
        Pages describing our plans, including the investor and grant summary, are for information only
        and are not an offer to sell or a solicitation of an offer to buy any security. Any investment
        would be made only through definitive documents and in compliance with applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Please do not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorized access to the sites or the simulator service;</li>
        <li>use automated means to launch simulator sessions in bulk or to evade session limits;</li>
        <li>submit unlawful, misleading or infringing content through our forms;</li>
        <li>misrepresent our content as an official agency product or operational data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content and reuse</h2>
      <p>
        Unless a page says otherwise, text, graphics and code on the sites are owned by {SITE_NAME} or used
        with permission. You may quote short excerpts with attribution and a link. Third-party images,
        videos, data and trademarks belong to their owners and are credited where used. Research data and
        code released under an open license are governed by that license.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
      <p>
        The sites link to and embed third-party sites and services, including Stripe, NASA, company
        websites and social media. We are not responsible for their content or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The sites are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, including
        accuracy, availability or fitness for a particular purpose. To the fullest extent permitted by
        law, {SITE_NAME} is not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for
        any loss arising from use of the sites, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the
        greater of the amount you paid us in the past twelve months or US$50.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The effective date above shows the latest version, and continued use
        of the sites after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
